course: dictionary
lesson: 5255
title: The many meanings of joke
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word joke has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. «Sharing silly jokes, like knock-knock jokes, builds friendship» means something you say to make people laugh. The clues are silly and friendship: here a joke is fun and shared.
explain: Joke can also be a verb, something you do with words to be funny. «Don't be cross, I was only joking!» Only and cross are your clues: the speaker is not being serious, so joking means saying things in fun.
explain: Sometimes a joke is not funny at all. «The test was a joke» means the test was silly or not taken seriously. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: A joke can also hurt. «If someone makes a racist or mean joke, do not laugh» tells you that a joke aimed at someone is not kind. Words carry feelings, so always check what a joke does to the people in it.
fact: Joke is a noun and a verb: you tell a joke, and you joke with your friends.
fact: «Knock-knock jokes» are short, silly jokes that many younger children love, and they help build friendships.
fact: Many jokes play on words, which is called a pun.
fact: Useful phrases: tell a joke, play a joke on someone, only joking, no joke (meaning serious), inside joke (a joke only a group understands).
fact: A joke that is racist or mean is not okay: do not laugh, say it is not okay, or tell an adult.
exercise: «Sharing silly jokes, like knock-knock jokes, builds friendship.» What is a joke in this sentence? | Something hidden in a box | A serious rule about sharing | *Something said to make people laugh | A test nobody takes seriously
exercise: Mum says, «I'm only joking!» What does she mean? | She is telling a true story | *She is not being serious | She is ordering dinner | She is very cross
exercise: The class says the spelling test «was a joke», because it was too easy and silly. What does joke mean here? | *Something not taken seriously | A sharp shout | A big laugh | A funny story
test: Ella's friend makes a mean joke about her new glasses. What should Ella do? | Tell an even meaner joke back | Hide the glasses | *Say it is not okay, or tell an adult | Laugh loudly with everyone
test: In «They joke about it all day», what kind of word is joke? | *A verb: to say things to be funny | A noun: a short funny story | A kind of sweet | A place to play
exam: Which phrase means the matter is serious, not a joke? | Only joking | Inside joke | Tell a joke | *No joke
